// @error return expects a value, got i32 | void
// The CHECKER now refuses a void arm in a value slot, so this program never reaches the
// emitter. `emitProgram: if-expression arm is empty, so it yields no value` is the
// emitter backstop behind that gate, unreachable through this route.
// BOUNDARY PIN (message wording, not coverage): the third way an if-expression arm can fail
// to produce a value — an EMPTY arm block, which has no value expression to find at all
// (`ifArmValueExpr` returns -1). Distinguished from an arm that HAS a last statement which
// yields nothing (`error-if-arm-ends-in-void-call.vl`, `error-if-arm-ends-in-statement.vl`),
// because "add a value" and "your call has no result" are different instructions.
function f(c: boolean) { return if c { 1 } else { } }
print(f(true))
